From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] auditd: serve audit_analytics

xnu's audit_triggers subsystem (mach/audit_triggers.defs, which the
project's audit_triggers.defs includes) has gained a second simpleroutine,
audit_analytics: the kernel sends the audit control port the signing ID and
name of each non-platform program that submits a record. Its MIG server
needs an implementation, and auditd had none, so it didn't link. Note the
caller in the debug log and return success.

--- a/openbsm/bin/auditd/auditd_darwin.c
+++ b/openbsm/bin/auditd/auditd_darwin.c
@@ -465,6 +465,23 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * Implementation of the audit_analytics() MIG simpleroutine, which xnu's
+ * audit_triggers subsystem has since gained: the kernel names the
+ * non-platform programs that submit audit records.  There is nothing to
+ * report them to; note them in the debug log.
+ */
+kern_return_t
+audit_analytics(mach_port_t __unused audit_port, string_t caller_id,
+    string_t caller_name)
+{
+
+	auditd_log_debug("audit record submitted by %s (%s)", caller_name,
+	    caller_id);
+
+	return (KERN_SUCCESS);
+}
+
+/*
  * When we get a signal, we are often not at a clean point.  So, little can
  * be done in the signal handler itself.  Instead,  we send a message to the
  * main servicing loop to do proper handling from a non-signal-handler
